1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,130
Sweetheart, on Christmas Day of two thousand

2
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:05,408
eleven, my son's new wife sat me

3
00:00:05,408 --> 00:00:07,542
at a card table in the laundry

4
00:00:07,542 --> 00:00:09,250
room, next to the dryer,

5
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:11,385
and served me a paper plate of

6
00:00:11,385 --> 00:00:14,089
leftovers while the rest of the family

7
00:00:14,089 --> 00:00:16,295
ate turkey on my own good china

8
00:00:16,295 --> 00:00:17,647
in the dining room.

9
00:00:17,827 --> 00:00:20,147
She said there just wasn't room for

10
00:00:20,147 --> 00:00:20,346
me.

11
00:00:20,526 --> 00:00:22,979
What she didn't know was whose name

12
00:00:22,979 --> 00:00:24,241
was on that house.

13
00:00:24,592 --> 00:00:27,101
Tonight I'm going to tell you everything

14
00:00:27,101 --> 00:00:28,920
that happened that Christmas,

15
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:30,739
what I heard her say about me

16
00:00:30,739 --> 00:00:32,307
through the kitchen door,

17
00:00:32,307 --> 00:00:34,189
and the one sentence I said at

18
00:00:34,189 --> 00:00:36,447
dessert that made the whole table go

19
00:00:36,447 --> 00:00:36,886
silent.

20
00:00:37,066 --> 00:00:38,048
Stay with me,

21
00:00:38,048 --> 00:00:41,221
honey, because the ending isn't what you'd

22
00:00:41,221 --> 00:00:43,638
expect from a sweet old grandma.

23
00:00:43,818 --> 00:00:45,884
And I'm still not sorry.

24
00:00:46,235 --> 00:00:48,582
My husband Harold and I bought that

25
00:00:48,582 --> 00:00:51,331
house on Maple Drive in nineteen seventy.

26
00:00:51,511 --> 00:00:54,092
Three bedrooms, a big oak tree,

27
00:00:54,092 --> 00:00:56,757
and a dining room big enough for

28
00:00:56,757 --> 00:00:57,339
twelve.

29
00:00:57,519 --> 00:00:59,888
We raised our children there.

30
00:01:00,068 --> 00:01:03,262
Harold carved forty-one Christmas turkeys at the

31
00:01:03,262 --> 00:01:04,526
head of that table.

32
00:01:04,706 --> 00:01:07,133
When he passed in two thousand eight,

33
00:01:07,133 --> 00:01:09,165
I was sixty-four and alone in a

34
00:01:09,165 --> 00:01:10,674
house full of memories.

35
00:01:11,023 --> 00:01:13,394
My son Gary was going through a

36
00:01:13,394 --> 00:01:14,541
hard time then.

37
00:01:14,721 --> 00:01:16,119
He'd lost his job,

38
00:01:16,119 --> 00:01:17,983
and he and his new wife,

39
00:01:17,983 --> 00:01:20,700
Tiffany, were behind on their rent.

40
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:23,690
So I did what mothers do.

41
00:01:23,870 --> 00:01:26,343
I said, come live with me.

42
00:01:26,523 --> 00:01:28,381
There's plenty of room.

43
00:01:28,561 --> 00:01:30,964
I gave them the master bedroom,

44
00:01:30,964 --> 00:01:32,359
Harold's and mine,

45
00:01:32,359 --> 00:01:34,994
and I moved into the little sewing

46
00:01:34,994 --> 00:01:36,312
room at the back,

47
00:01:36,312 --> 00:01:38,870
because I didn't need much space.

48
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:42,723
Now, honey, here's the thing nobody told

49
00:01:42,723 --> 00:01:43,423
Tiffany.

50
00:01:43,603 --> 00:01:45,011
When Harold died,

51
00:01:45,011 --> 00:01:47,330
the house didn't go to Gary.

52
00:01:47,510 --> 00:01:48,948
It was mine,

53
00:01:48,948 --> 00:01:51,585
paid off, every brick.

54
00:01:51,765 --> 00:01:52,833
Gary knew.

55
00:01:53,013 --> 00:01:54,186
Tiffany didn't.

56
00:01:54,366 --> 00:01:56,747
And somewhere in those three years,

57
00:01:56,747 --> 00:01:59,401
she started telling people it was their

58
00:01:59,401 --> 00:02:01,851
house, and that they were letting me

59
00:02:01,851 --> 00:02:02,191
stay.

60
00:02:02,371 --> 00:02:04,289
In a minute I'll tell you how

61
00:02:04,289 --> 00:02:05,413
I found that out.

62
00:02:05,762 --> 00:02:07,406
It happened slowly,

63
00:02:07,406 --> 00:02:11,126
sweetheart, the way these things always do.

64
00:02:11,306 --> 00:02:13,546
First my good china moved to a

65
00:02:13,546 --> 00:02:15,637
high shelf I couldn't reach.

66
00:02:15,817 --> 00:02:18,341
Then my recipe box went to the

67
00:02:18,341 --> 00:02:20,948
garage, because it was clutter.

68
00:02:21,128 --> 00:02:23,417
Then my chair at the head of

69
00:02:23,417 --> 00:02:25,542
the table, Harold's chair,

70
00:02:25,542 --> 00:02:27,177
became Gary's chair.

71
00:02:27,357 --> 00:02:30,502
Then my friends from church stopped coming

72
00:02:30,502 --> 00:02:33,272
by, because Tiffany always said I was

73
00:02:33,272 --> 00:02:33,870
resting.

74
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:36,055
Then there were the comments.

75
00:02:36,235 --> 00:02:38,777
Mom, you're getting forgetful.

76
00:02:38,957 --> 00:02:41,384
Mom, maybe you shouldn't drive.

77
00:02:41,564 --> 00:02:43,877
Mom, have you thought about one of

78
00:02:43,877 --> 00:02:45,918
those nice places for seniors?

79
00:02:46,098 --> 00:02:48,536
And I'd catch Tiffany looking at me

80
00:02:48,536 --> 00:02:49,859
across the kitchen,

81
00:02:49,859 --> 00:02:51,740
the way you look at a piece

82
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:54,457
of furniture you're planning to get rid

83
00:02:54,457 --> 00:02:54,666
of.

84
00:02:54,846 --> 00:02:56,692
Gary never said a word.

85
00:02:56,872 --> 00:02:59,089
He just looked at his phone.

86
00:02:59,439 --> 00:03:01,912
That fall, I found a brochure on

87
00:03:01,912 --> 00:03:03,457
the kitchen counter.

88
00:03:03,637 --> 00:03:05,912
Sunny Pines Assisted Living.

89
00:03:06,092 --> 00:03:08,751
Somebody had circled the price,

90
00:03:08,751 --> 00:03:10,982
and written in the margin,

91
00:03:10,982 --> 00:03:12,183
in purple pen,

92
00:03:12,183 --> 00:03:13,984
Tiffany's purple pen,

93
00:03:13,984 --> 00:03:15,871
the words, sell house,

94
00:03:15,871 --> 00:03:16,986
pay for this,

95
00:03:16,986 --> 00:03:18,016
rest for us.

96
00:03:18,196 --> 00:03:20,732
I put it back exactly where I

97
00:03:20,732 --> 00:03:22,131
found it, honey.

98
00:03:22,311 --> 00:03:24,366
And I didn't say a word.

99
00:03:24,546 --> 00:03:27,124
I just started paying attention.

100
00:03:27,474 --> 00:03:30,496
If you're enjoying Grandma's story,

101
00:03:30,496 --> 00:03:32,828
tap the like button for me,

102
00:03:32,828 --> 00:03:33,778
sweetheart.

103
00:03:33,958 --> 00:03:37,290
It helps more people find these stories.

104
00:03:37,470 --> 00:03:38,992
On Christmas morning,

105
00:03:38,992 --> 00:03:41,022
Tiffany's whole family came.

106
00:03:41,202 --> 00:03:43,297
Her parents, her sister,

107
00:03:43,297 --> 00:03:45,130
her sister's husband,

108
00:03:45,130 --> 00:03:46,439
three children.

109
00:03:46,619 --> 00:03:47,989
Fourteen people.

110
00:03:48,169 --> 00:03:50,204
And I'd been up since five,

111
00:03:50,204 --> 00:03:52,089
making Harold's stuffing,

112
00:03:52,089 --> 00:03:53,446
my mother's rolls,

113
00:03:53,446 --> 00:03:54,426
and two pies,

114
00:03:54,426 --> 00:03:57,517
because I'd made Christmas dinner in that

115
00:03:57,517 --> 00:03:59,628
kitchen for forty-one years.

116
00:03:59,978 --> 00:04:01,157
At two o'clock,

117
00:04:01,157 --> 00:04:03,043
I carried in the turkey,

118
00:04:03,043 --> 00:04:04,851
and I went to sit down,

119
00:04:04,851 --> 00:04:06,816
and there wasn't a chair.

120
00:04:06,996 --> 00:04:10,908
Fourteen chairs, fourteen place cards in Tiffany's

121
00:04:10,908 --> 00:04:13,489
purple pen, and none of them said

122
00:04:13,489 --> 00:04:13,880
Ruth.

123
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:15,999
Tiffany smiled at me,

124
00:04:15,999 --> 00:04:17,753
a big bright smile,

125
00:04:17,753 --> 00:04:18,953
and said, oh,

126
00:04:18,953 --> 00:04:21,537
Mom, we're so tight in here.

127
00:04:21,717 --> 00:04:23,653
I set you up a little spot

128
00:04:23,653 --> 00:04:25,142
in the laundry room.

129
00:04:25,322 --> 00:04:26,576
It's cozy.

130
00:04:26,756 --> 00:04:27,997
You won't mind,

131
00:04:27,997 --> 00:04:28,741
will you?

132
00:04:29,092 --> 00:04:31,652
Everybody looked at their plates,

133
00:04:31,652 --> 00:04:32,505
sweetheart.

134
00:04:32,685 --> 00:04:34,475
Her mother looked at me with a

135
00:04:34,475 --> 00:04:35,251
little smirk.

136
00:04:35,431 --> 00:04:36,324
And my son,

137
00:04:36,324 --> 00:04:37,217
my own son,

138
00:04:37,217 --> 00:04:39,895
whom I carried and nursed and sat

139
00:04:39,895 --> 00:04:42,168
up with through every fever,

140
00:04:42,168 --> 00:04:44,685
looked down at his lap and said

141
00:04:44,685 --> 00:04:45,334
nothing.

142
00:04:45,514 --> 00:04:46,487
So I said,

143
00:04:46,487 --> 00:04:47,849
of course not,

144
00:04:47,849 --> 00:04:48,335
dear.

145
00:04:48,515 --> 00:04:51,199
And I walked into the laundry room,

146
00:04:51,199 --> 00:04:53,269
and I sat down at that card

147
00:04:53,269 --> 00:04:55,110
table next to the dryer.

148
00:04:55,290 --> 00:04:57,546
Remember that card table,

149
00:04:57,546 --> 00:04:58,088
honey.

150
00:04:58,268 --> 00:05:00,369
You'll see why at the end.

151
00:05:00,719 --> 00:05:03,357
The laundry room door was right next

152
00:05:03,357 --> 00:05:04,457
to the kitchen.

153
00:05:04,637 --> 00:05:07,301
And when Tiffany and her sister went

154
00:05:07,301 --> 00:05:08,781
in to get the gravy,

155
00:05:08,781 --> 00:05:10,186
I heard every word.

156
00:05:10,366 --> 00:05:11,818
Her sister said,

157
00:05:11,818 --> 00:05:14,267
Tiff, that's kind of harsh.

158
00:05:14,447 --> 00:05:17,225
And Tiffany laughed and said,

159
00:05:17,225 --> 00:05:18,279
oh, please.

160
00:05:18,459 --> 00:05:21,059
She'll be in Sunny Pines by March.

161
00:05:21,239 --> 00:05:24,374
Gary's already talking to a realtor.

162
00:05:24,554 --> 00:05:27,178
This house is worth three hundred thousand.

163
00:05:27,358 --> 00:05:30,479
Next Christmas, we'll have the whole place

164
00:05:30,479 --> 00:05:31,445
to ourselves.

165
00:05:31,795 --> 00:05:34,044
I sat there with my paper plate,

166
00:05:34,044 --> 00:05:36,363
honey, and I looked at the dryer,

167
00:05:36,363 --> 00:05:38,261
and I thought about Harold.

168
00:05:38,441 --> 00:05:40,744
I thought about him carrying me over

169
00:05:40,744 --> 00:05:41,704
that threshold.

170
00:05:41,884 --> 00:05:43,381
Painting the nursery.

171
00:05:43,561 --> 00:05:46,183
Hanging the tire swing on the oak

172
00:05:46,183 --> 00:05:46,580
tree.

173
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:48,269
I didn't cry.

174
00:05:48,449 --> 00:05:50,330
I'm a Mansfield girl.

175
00:05:50,510 --> 00:05:52,890
My mother didn't raise a crier.

176
00:05:53,070 --> 00:05:54,460
Instead, I got up,

177
00:05:54,460 --> 00:05:56,775
and I went to the sewing room,

178
00:05:56,775 --> 00:05:58,782
and I made one phone call.

179
00:05:59,133 --> 00:06:01,292
I called Walter Simms.

180
00:06:01,472 --> 00:06:04,392
Walter had been Harold's lawyer for thirty

181
00:06:04,392 --> 00:06:07,103
years, and he lived three streets over.

182
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:08,604
I said, Walter,

183
00:06:08,604 --> 00:06:11,335
I'm sorry to call on Christmas.

184
00:06:11,515 --> 00:06:13,795
Could you come by at four o'clock

185
00:06:13,795 --> 00:06:14,348
for pie?

186
00:06:14,528 --> 00:06:16,199
And bring the folder.

187
00:06:16,379 --> 00:06:19,181
Walter didn't ask a single question,

188
00:06:19,181 --> 00:06:20,037
sweetheart.

189
00:06:20,217 --> 00:06:21,298
He just said,

190
00:06:21,298 --> 00:06:24,375
Ruth, I've been waiting for this call

191
00:06:24,375 --> 00:06:25,290
for a year.

192
00:06:25,470 --> 00:06:27,072
I'll be there at four.

193
00:06:27,423 --> 00:06:28,838
At four o'clock,

194
00:06:28,838 --> 00:06:30,430
the doorbell rang.

195
00:06:30,610 --> 00:06:32,037
Tiffany opened it,

196
00:06:32,037 --> 00:06:35,446
annoyed, and Walter Simms walked right past

197
00:06:35,446 --> 00:06:37,904
her into the dining room in his

198
00:06:37,904 --> 00:06:39,094
good gray suit,

199
00:06:39,094 --> 00:06:41,314
carrying a fat brown folder.

200
00:06:41,494 --> 00:06:43,526
He said, merry Christmas,

201
00:06:43,526 --> 00:06:44,338
everybody.

202
00:06:44,518 --> 00:06:45,877
Where's Ruth?

203
00:06:46,057 --> 00:06:48,288
And I came out of that laundry

204
00:06:48,288 --> 00:06:51,041
room, honey, carrying two of my pies,

205
00:06:51,041 --> 00:06:53,124
and I set them right down on

206
00:06:53,124 --> 00:06:54,091
my own table.

207
00:06:54,441 --> 00:06:56,217
Tiffany said, Mom,

208
00:06:56,217 --> 00:06:57,401
who is this?

209
00:06:57,581 --> 00:06:58,681
And I said,

210
00:06:58,681 --> 00:07:00,181
this is Walter,

211
00:07:00,181 --> 00:07:00,681
dear.

212
00:07:00,861 --> 00:07:02,173
He's my lawyer.

213
00:07:02,353 --> 00:07:04,491
And then I said the sentence I

214
00:07:04,491 --> 00:07:05,418
promised you.

215
00:07:05,598 --> 00:07:06,907
I said, Tiffany,

216
00:07:06,907 --> 00:07:09,116
I heard you in the kitchen.

217
00:07:09,296 --> 00:07:12,017
And since you're so worried about room

218
00:07:12,017 --> 00:07:13,020
at this table,

219
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:15,669
I thought we'd talk about whose table

220
00:07:15,669 --> 00:07:16,099
it is.

221
00:07:16,279 --> 00:07:19,264
Fourteen people stopped chewing at the same

222
00:07:19,264 --> 00:07:19,611
time.

223
00:07:19,791 --> 00:07:22,130
You could've heard a pin drop on

224
00:07:22,130 --> 00:07:23,007
that carpet.

225
00:07:23,358 --> 00:07:26,030
Walter opened the folder and laid the

226
00:07:26,030 --> 00:07:28,485
deed right on top of the cranberry

227
00:07:28,485 --> 00:07:28,919
sauce.

228
00:07:29,099 --> 00:07:30,585
He read it out loud.

229
00:07:30,765 --> 00:07:33,613
Property of Ruth Ellen Miller,

230
00:07:33,613 --> 00:07:35,892
sole owner, no mortgage,

231
00:07:35,892 --> 00:07:36,651
no lien.

232
00:07:36,831 --> 00:07:39,211
And then he read the second paper,

233
00:07:39,211 --> 00:07:41,872
a letter I'd signed two months before,

234
00:07:41,872 --> 00:07:43,762
when I found that brochure.

235
00:07:43,942 --> 00:07:46,695
It gave Gary and Tiffany thirty days'

236
00:07:46,695 --> 00:07:48,853
notice to find a new place to

237
00:07:48,853 --> 00:07:49,225
live.

238
00:07:49,575 --> 00:07:51,311
Tiffany went white,

239
00:07:51,311 --> 00:07:53,777
then red, then white again.

240
00:07:53,957 --> 00:07:56,295
She said, you can't do that,

241
00:07:56,295 --> 00:07:57,464
you're senile.

242
00:07:57,644 --> 00:08:00,364
And Walter smiled and pulled out one

243
00:08:00,364 --> 00:08:03,085
more paper, a letter from my doctor,

244
00:08:03,085 --> 00:08:04,672
dated that same week,

245
00:08:04,672 --> 00:08:07,393
saying I was in excellent health and

246
00:08:07,393 --> 00:08:09,207
of perfectly sound mind.

247
00:08:09,387 --> 00:08:10,962
Walter said, ma'am,

248
00:08:10,962 --> 00:08:12,951
she's sharper than I am.

249
00:08:13,131 --> 00:08:15,633
Tiffany's mother picked up her coat and

250
00:08:15,633 --> 00:08:16,916
left without a word.

251
00:08:17,267 --> 00:08:19,799
And then my son finally looked up

252
00:08:19,799 --> 00:08:20,796
from his lap.

253
00:08:20,976 --> 00:08:22,543
He said, Mom.

254
00:08:22,723 --> 00:08:25,475
Mom, I didn't know she said that.

255
00:08:25,655 --> 00:08:26,669
And I said,

256
00:08:26,669 --> 00:08:30,078
Gary, you knew about the place cards.

257
00:08:30,258 --> 00:08:32,441
You knew about the laundry room.

258
00:08:32,621 --> 00:08:34,537
You knew about the realtor.

259
00:08:34,717 --> 00:08:36,605
You didn't have to say the words

260
00:08:36,605 --> 00:08:37,608
to be part of it.

261
00:08:37,788 --> 00:08:39,854
Your father would be ashamed.

262
00:08:40,034 --> 00:08:41,793
And that, sweetheart,

263
00:08:41,793 --> 00:08:44,307
is when my son started to cry.

264
00:08:44,657 --> 00:08:46,293
So far, the house,

265
00:08:46,293 --> 00:08:49,110
the brochure, the laundry room,

266
00:08:49,110 --> 00:08:50,473
and the folder.

267
00:08:50,653 --> 00:08:53,173
But here's the part nobody believes.

268
00:08:53,353 --> 00:08:55,488
I didn't throw my son out to

269
00:08:55,488 --> 00:08:56,174
be cruel.

270
00:08:56,354 --> 00:08:58,119
I want you to know that.

271
00:08:58,299 --> 00:09:00,648
I did it because I loved him,

272
00:09:00,648 --> 00:09:03,969
and because I'd watched him disappear for

273
00:09:03,969 --> 00:09:06,805
three years, into his phone and his

274
00:09:06,805 --> 00:09:09,154
excuses and his wife's plans.

275
00:09:09,334 --> 00:09:11,274
And sometimes, honey,

276
00:09:11,274 --> 00:09:13,676
love has to slam the door.

277
00:09:14,026 --> 00:09:16,858
Tiffany left Gary in three weeks.

278
00:09:17,038 --> 00:09:19,321
Once there was no house to sell,

279
00:09:19,321 --> 00:09:21,961
she didn't see much point in staying.

280
00:09:22,141 --> 00:09:23,544
She took the car,

281
00:09:23,544 --> 00:09:26,349
the television, and my good china,

282
00:09:26,349 --> 00:09:28,329
which I never saw again.

283
00:09:28,509 --> 00:09:31,452
Gary moved into a little apartment over

284
00:09:31,452 --> 00:09:32,735
a hardware store.

285
00:09:32,915 --> 00:09:34,406
And for a whole year,

286
00:09:34,406 --> 00:09:35,969
my son didn't call me.

287
00:09:36,149 --> 00:09:38,548
That was the hardest year of my

288
00:09:38,548 --> 00:09:39,864
life, sweetheart.

289
00:09:40,044 --> 00:09:41,913
Harder than losing Harold.

290
00:09:42,263 --> 00:09:45,177
But something happened in that little apartment.

291
00:09:45,357 --> 00:09:47,676
Gary got a job at the hardware

292
00:09:47,676 --> 00:09:48,991
store downstairs.

293
00:09:49,171 --> 00:09:51,736
Then he became assistant manager.

294
00:09:51,916 --> 00:09:54,389
He started going back to church.

295
00:09:54,569 --> 00:09:56,269
And the next December,

296
00:09:56,269 --> 00:09:58,278
the week before Christmas,

297
00:09:58,278 --> 00:09:59,591
my doorbell rang,

298
00:09:59,591 --> 00:10:01,677
and there was my son on the

299
00:10:01,677 --> 00:10:03,145
porch, in the snow,

300
00:10:03,145 --> 00:10:05,849
holding a card table he'd bought at

301
00:10:05,849 --> 00:10:07,317
the hardware store.

302
00:10:07,667 --> 00:10:08,630
He said, Mom,

303
00:10:08,630 --> 00:10:10,629
I want to sit at this table

304
00:10:10,629 --> 00:10:11,370
this year.

305
00:10:11,550 --> 00:10:13,118
In the laundry room.

306
00:10:13,298 --> 00:10:15,202
You sit at the head of the

307
00:10:15,202 --> 00:10:16,521
dining room table,

308
00:10:16,521 --> 00:10:17,547
where Dad sat.

309
00:10:17,727 --> 00:10:19,758
And I'll eat by the dryer and

310
00:10:19,758 --> 00:10:21,860
think about what I let happen.

311
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:23,587
I said, Gary,

312
00:10:23,587 --> 00:10:25,372
don't be silly.

313
00:10:25,552 --> 00:10:26,794
Get in here.

314
00:10:26,974 --> 00:10:29,207
And my son put his arms around

315
00:10:29,207 --> 00:10:30,471
me on that porch,

316
00:10:30,471 --> 00:10:32,406
and he held on like he was

317
00:10:32,406 --> 00:10:33,522
five years old.

318
00:10:33,873 --> 00:10:36,612
That Christmas, we set the big table

319
00:10:36,612 --> 00:10:37,448
for twelve.

320
00:10:37,628 --> 00:10:40,440
My daughter came from Indiana with her

321
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:40,810
kids.

322
00:10:40,990 --> 00:10:42,801
My friends from church.

323
00:10:42,981 --> 00:10:45,268
Walter Simms and his wife.

324
00:10:45,448 --> 00:10:47,942
And the very last place card,

325
00:10:47,942 --> 00:10:49,834
in my own handwriting,

326
00:10:49,834 --> 00:10:52,414
said Gary, right next to mine.

327
00:10:52,594 --> 00:10:54,510
We used paper plates,

328
00:10:54,510 --> 00:10:57,157
because Tiffany had my china.

329
00:10:57,337 --> 00:10:58,730
Nobody cared.

330
00:10:58,910 --> 00:11:01,278
It was the best Christmas dinner in

331
00:11:01,278 --> 00:11:03,240
that house since Harold died.

332
00:11:03,591 --> 00:11:06,758
Gary owns that hardware store now,

333
00:11:06,758 --> 00:11:07,317
honey.

334
00:11:07,497 --> 00:11:10,292
He's married to a wonderful woman named

335
00:11:10,292 --> 00:11:13,230
Linda, a schoolteacher who calls me every

336
00:11:13,230 --> 00:11:13,732
Sunday.

337
00:11:13,912 --> 00:11:15,527
And every Christmas,

338
00:11:15,527 --> 00:11:17,951
he sets up that old card table

339
00:11:17,951 --> 00:11:19,566
in the laundry room.

340
00:11:19,746 --> 00:11:21,000
Not to eat at.

341
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:23,107
He puts the pies on it.

342
00:11:23,287 --> 00:11:25,168
He says it reminds him of the

343
00:11:25,168 --> 00:11:27,374
day his mother taught him the most

344
00:11:27,374 --> 00:11:29,255
important lesson of his life.

345
00:11:29,605 --> 00:11:32,184
Here's what I want you to remember,

346
00:11:32,184 --> 00:11:32,995
sweetheart.

347
00:11:33,175 --> 00:11:35,973
Being kind doesn't mean being a doormat.

348
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:38,864
You can love your children with your

349
00:11:38,864 --> 00:11:40,823
whole heart and still say,

350
00:11:40,823 --> 00:11:42,329
no, not in my house.

351
00:11:42,509 --> 00:11:45,447
Too many grandmothers I know are sitting

352
00:11:45,447 --> 00:11:47,650
in the laundry room right now,

353
00:11:47,650 --> 00:11:48,604
being polite.

354
00:11:48,784 --> 00:11:50,340
Don't you be one of them.

355
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:52,064
You built that table.

356
00:11:52,244 --> 00:11:53,638
You get a chair.

357
00:11:53,988 --> 00:11:55,975
Tell me in the comments,

358
00:11:55,975 --> 00:11:56,472
honey.

359
00:11:56,652 --> 00:11:58,772
Was I too hard on my son,

360
00:11:58,772 --> 00:12:00,298
or did he need it?

361
00:12:00,478 --> 00:12:02,869
Be honest with Grandma.

362
00:12:03,049 --> 00:12:05,296
And if anyone ever made you feel

363
00:12:05,296 --> 00:12:07,402
like a guest in your own home,

364
00:12:07,402 --> 00:12:09,086
I want to hear about it.

365
00:12:09,266 --> 00:12:11,767
There are more of my family's stories

366
00:12:11,767 --> 00:12:14,133
in the playlist right there on your

367
00:12:14,133 --> 00:12:16,228
screen, and I'll see you in the

368
00:12:16,228 --> 00:12:16,836
next one.

369
00:12:17,016 --> 00:12:19,048
Good night, sweetheart.
